<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Gentech half yr share sinks deeper, no div.</title>
<headline>Gentech half yr share sinks deeper, no div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended Aug 31 1996</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     38.7  loss  vs   23.9  loss</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   21.97 loss  vs   13.59 loss</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   22.39 loss  vs   14.21 loss</p>
<p>    Tax			  0.42	 vs    0.62</p>
<p>    Interest paid	    6.18	 vs    3.95</p>
<p>    Turnover		 160.29	 vs  188.42</p>
<p>Full name: General Technologies Ltd (electronics)</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said that following its sale of wholly-owned subsidiary Gentrade and two other subsidiaries last week, Gentech was now constituted as a cash shell. As a result, its Johannesburg Stock Exchange listing had been transferred to the &quot;cash companies&quot; sector of the exchange.</p>
<p>It said that it was intended to find an appropriate buyer to buy Allied Electronics Corp's (Altron) and Power Technologies Ltd's (Powertech) shares in the Gentech cash shell.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
